+/* openmmo: whether either of the two menus above is on the screen.
+ *
+ * Both of them are SysTasks that free themselves, and the only thing that knows
+ * one has finished is the static it clears on its way out. On a cartridge
+ * nothing has to ask: an underground player is walked by a keypad the group's
+ * server stops sending while they are talking, so the field takes itself back.
+ * Here the local player is walked by the overworld's own input path and the
+ * field is paused for the length of a conversation instead, so the moment it
+ * ends has to be observable, and it is also when the other end of the
+ * conversation has to be told. mmo/mods/openmmo/src/openmmo_underground.c. */
+BOOL UndergroundTalk_IsActive(void)
+{
+    return sCurrentTalkMenu != NULL || sCurrentResponseMenu != NULL;
+}
